course: dictionary
lesson: 10019
title: Tenancy: renting a home
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about homes, money and rules. You can work out what they mean from the words around them. «Renters sign a tenancy and pay a deposit that comes back if the home is left in good condition.» Renters are people who rent, and a deposit is money you pay up front. So a tenancy must be something you sign to rent a home.
explain: «A tenancy is the agreement to rent a home for a set time; at the end the landlord can offer a new one or ask the family to leave.» Here the sentence tells you what a tenancy is. Try the check: swap in "the agreement to rent a home for a set time" and see if it still makes sense. It does, so you have found the meaning.
explain: Tenancy can mean two things. It can be the agreement to rent, or the length of time you rent a place. Look for «a six-month tenancy»: the words six-month show it is a length of time. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence before you decide.
fact: Tenancy means the right to live in or use a house, flat, land or shop that you rent from the owner.
fact: Tenancy can also mean the time you rent a place, as in «a six-month tenancy».
fact: Tenancy is a noun. The plural is tenancies.
fact: In everyday life, a family rents a home under a tenancy agreement with a landlord.
fact: In maths problems, a tenancy can be worked out as rent per month multiplied by the number of months.
exercise: «Renters sign a tenancy and pay a deposit that comes back if the home is left in good condition.» What is a tenancy? | *The right to rent a home from the owner | A person who fixes broken roofs | A type of garden shed | A kind of deposit
exercise: Nadia says, «We have a six-month tenancy.» What does tenancy mean here? | A broken window | *The time the family rents the home for | The owner of the house | The money that comes back at the end
exercise: «Families move house for many reasons: a new job, more room, a cheaper rent, or because a tenancy ends.» Which reason is about money? | A new job | Because a tenancy ends | More room | *A cheaper rent
test: «A tenancy is the agreement to rent a home for a set time.» What does the word agreement tell you about a tenancy? | *It is a promise between the renter and the landlord | It is a pile of old furniture | It is a game played in the garden | It is a sort of holiday
test: In a maths problem, how do you work out the cost of a tenancy? | Add the deposit and the landlord's name | Rent per month plus the number of months | *Rent per month multiplied by the number of months | Number of months divided by the rent
exam: Which phrase means the length of time you rent a home? | A home deposit | A tenancy agreement | *A six-month tenancy | A landlord's letter
